---

## First Run

Run the following command to generate your local tool index:

```powershell
# Windows (PowerShell)
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "skills/scripts/refresh-tool-index.ps1"
```

```bash
# Linux / macOS / Kali
bash skills/scripts/refresh-tool-index.sh
```

---

## Generated Format

Windows (PowerShell) generates an 8-column table:
| Tool | Skill owner | Purpose | Available | Path | Version | Source | Script reference |

Linux/macOS (Bash) generates a 7-column table:
| Tool | Skill | Purpose | Available | Path | Version | Install hint |

Both include a "Capability Status" subtable with MCP registration status and service reachability checks.

